    var faqPairs = new (string Q, string A)[]
    {
        ("Should we hire more courts than we need so nobody sits out?",
         "Usually no. An extra court costs the same every week whether it is busy or not, and sit-outs are more often a rotation problem than a capacity one. Work out what your busiest realistic night looks like, hire for that, and fix the queue rather than buying your way out of it."),
        ("Can we sublet spare courts to another group?",
         "Ask, because we cannot tell you. No operator we looked at publishes its block-booking terms, so we have no basis for saying what is normal here. It is worth asking directly: a second group sharing your block is one of the few things that lowers your cost per player at all."),
        ("Is it cheaper to run two shorter nights or one long one?",
         "Two nights almost never costs less, because the price is per court-hour either way and you double your exposure to peak pricing. It can still be the right call for other reasons, such as splitting standards or fitting more members into a small hall, but treat it as a membership decision rather than a saving."),
        ("Do we have to be affiliated to hire a council hall?",
         "Not usually for the booking itself, but a centre will normally want to see evidence of public liability cover before letting a regular block, and affiliation is a common route to that. Check what your own affiliation actually includes, in its current wording, rather than assuming it covers every person on court."),
        ("What if the centre wants to move us to a different night?",
         "This is why the variation and cancellation terms matter as much as the price. Ask what notice they must give to move or cancel a session, and what happens to sessions you have already paid for. If the answer is vague, get it in writing before you commit to a series."),
        ("Would registering as a CASC make court hire cheaper?",
         "Not directly. CASC status affects rates relief and tax treatment for the club itself, not what a leisure centre charges you. It matters more if your club owns or leases its own facility, which is a different situation from hiring one."),
        ("What about hiring a school hall during the holidays?",
         "School lettings are often the cheapest option in a given town, but term-time and holiday availability are usually governed separately, and a hall available in June may be shut in August. If your season runs through the summer, ask about holiday access before you move.")
    };

    var articleJsonLd = GuideSchema.Article(
