      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>If you are hiring courts because you are setting a club up from scratch, the venue is one of five things you need at once. <a href="/guides/how-to-start-a-badminton-club">How to start a badminton club</a> covers the others: players, kit, fees and your first sessions.</p>
      <p>Once the hall is booked, your cost per player depends entirely on how full the courts are. <a href="/guides/fair-court-time-busy-club-night">Giving everyone fair court time on a busy night</a> deals with the sit-out problem directly, and <a href="/guides/how-to-run-a-badminton-club-night">the complete organiser's checklist</a> covers the rest of the evening.</p>
      <p>The next question after "what does the hall cost" is usually "what do we buy with the rest of it". Shuttles are the other recurring line, and <a href="/guides/feather-vs-nylon-shuttlecocks">feather vs nylon: what your club should buy</a> works out the cost per session the same way this guide works out the cost per court.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We do not hire out courts, we are not tax advisers, and we have never negotiated a court-hire contract. The prices here come from a survey we ran ourselves: on 26 August 2026 we read the published rate cards and booking pages of 24 UK venues and recorded every figure with its source and its fee year. Eighteen sell a comparable per-court unit and those are the ones in the chart and table.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0">The VAT section is compiled from HMRC's published notices, and where the treatment depends on your supplier or your building we have said so rather than picking the answer that sounds most useful. Where we could not find a source we have said that too: no operator publishes its block-booking terms, no published figure exists for what clubs actually negotiate off list price, and we found no published badminton rate at any Northern Ireland venue.</p>
